! ------------------- Class definition for GRDelayedSend
expectvalue /Class
doit
GRObject subclass: 'GRDelayedSend'
	instVarNames: #( receiver message)
	classVars: #()
	classInstVars: #()
	poolDictionaries: #()
	category: 'Grease-Core-Utilities'
	inDictionary: ZincGlobals
	options: #()

%
expectvalue /Class
doit
GRDelayedSend comment: 
'A GRDelayedSend is a future message send of a message to an object. Some of the arguments can be predefined. Instances are intended to be interchangeable with blocks.This class should conform the ANSI (block) valuable protocol. Unlike a block, a GRDelayedSend is not a closure so doesn''t hold onto the method context. GRDelayedSend provides similar, but portable, functionality to Pharo''s MessageSend.This is an abstract class. Use the methods in the ''instance-creation'' protocol on the class side to create intances.Instance Variables	receiver:		<Object>	selector:		<Symbol>receiver	- the object receiving the messageselector	- the message selector sent to the receiver'
%
expectvalue /Class
doit
GRDelayedSend category: 'Grease-Core-Utilities'
%
